    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44701" root="&#xA;                        وقى&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاهُ ٱللّٰهُ السُّوْءَ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>God preserved him from
evil.</i> (Msb.) See a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَقَشَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاكَ اللّٰهُ كُلَّ مَحْذُور</span>
                        <i>God preserve thee from
all fear:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَحْذُورٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِهْ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَقَّ</span>,
are imperatives [meaning <i>Be thou cautious</i>].
(JK.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِ عَلَى ظَلْعِكَ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلَعَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَقَاهُ</span> and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِتَّقَاهُ</span></b>  both signify <i>He was cautious of it;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَذِرَهُ</span>. (K.)

